capability open/default-application  a URL or a file opened in the application the user's system keeps for it
  heroes  os.open_url, os.open_path
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  webbrowser.open, webbrowser.open_new, webbrowser.open_new_tab, os.startfile (Windows alone)
  note    added 2026-11-17, from the community census: `open` on Darwin and `xdg-open` on every other POSIX, started by `posix_spawn` with the target as their one argument, no shell between, the signals at their defaults, and waited for; `ShellExecuteW` with the verb `open` on Windows (`hero_sys_open`). A URL is checked first: `http`, `https` or `mailto` alone, since another scheme starts whatever program registered it, no white space and no control character, a host after `//`; a path must name something, asked before the launcher runs, and one that begins with `-` is handed as `./-...` so no launcher reads it as an option. Python's webbrowser chooses among browsers and falls back to a text browser; here the system's own choice is the one, and a new window or tab is the browser's to decide. Run on this Mac on a path that is not there (`open` printed its refusal and ended 1, `failed`); a URL and a file actually opened: unrun, since a test that opens a window on the machine running it is not a test to run unattended

